export anchor HighContrastProfessionalStyle:
    number: 223
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: High contrast professional
    idea: Strict black on white with heavy 2px rules, large plain type and no colour at all except a bright yellow focus ring, built first for people who need maximum contrast and still calm enough for daily work.
    base: light
    palette:
        black: #111111, text, rules, the header, primary button, this week bars and the Behind chip
        white: #ffffff, the page, fields, text on black and last week bars
        grey: #f2f2f2, reserved for disabled surfaces, never behind text that matters
        mid: #4a4a4a, placeholder text only
        yellow: #ffd60a, the focus ring, never text and never decoration
    type:
        One stack, Atkinson Hyperlegible, Segoe UI, system-ui, Roboto,
        Helvetica Neue, Arial. The greeting is 36px 800, KPI figures 52px
        800, section titles 26px 800 over a 4px rule, project names 17px
        800 underlined, body 16px and meta 15px 700. Nothing is smaller
        than 15px.
    layout:
        A black masthead holds a white square mark with a black check, the
        brand in white, a white search field, a white New project button,
        a square outlined bell with a count and a round outlined initials
        disc with Mara Okafor. Under it the nav is a row of six equal
        boxed links split by 2px black rules, the current one filled black
        with white underlined text. The body is one 1120px column. The
        greeting Hello, Mara sits over the date, then a box with a 3px
        border and a 12px left bar reads 4 tasks are overdue with a clock
        and a Show overdue tasks link. The four KPIs are one bordered box
        split into four cells by 2px rules, each a label over a 52px
        figure, the overdue cell inverted black. Projects is a full width
        table with 2px row rules, columns for project and department, a
        bordered status chip, a bordered progress bar with percent, tasks
        done and due date with days left. Last, two columns hold the chart
        with paired bars by weekday, last week white with a black outline
        and this week solid black with values on top, and a numbered list
        of recent activity with boxed numbers. Below 760px the nav becomes
        a three by two grid of boxes, KPIs go two by two, table rows become
        stacked blocks and the chart scrolls sideways.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 44px minimum targets, 14px row padding, 40 to 48px between sections.
    density: Medium low. One column for summary and table, then chart and activity side by side.
    corners: Square everywhere. Only the avatar and the notification count are round.
    borders: 2px black on every box, rule and row. 4px under section titles, a 12px left bar on the overdue note and 8px over the style sheet.
    shadows: None. The only box shadow is the yellow focus ring.
    icons:
        Line icons at 2px stroke sized at 1.25em. Status shapes are 20px,
        an outlined circle with a check, an outlined triangle with a bang
        and a solid square with a down arrow in an inverted chip for
        Behind, each with its word in a bordered chip.
    focus: A 3px black outline with a 7px yellow ring outside it on white, and a 3px yellow outline on black.
    tone: Direct and literal, such as Hello, Mara, 4 tasks are overdue and Show overdue tasks.
